                <pb facs="0910" n="898" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg898"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.51 Frozen Credits/9618: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-12T19:00:00-04:00">March 12, 1943—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>286. Your no. 402, March 3, 10 a.m. and 424, March 4, 7 p.m.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d859-f1"/> Department appreciates progress being made in program of
                    economic and financial controls in Chile, and Embassy should continue to render
                    all proper assistance desired by Chilean Government. However, such assistance
                    should under no circumstances extend to preparation of draft laws or decrees by
                    the Embassy for consideration and possible enactment by Chilean Government. Such
                    a procedure, especially in view of del PedregaPs connection with this matter,
                    might have unfortunate repercussions. There is no objection to Embassy’s making
                    appropriate comments on decrees drafted by Chilean Government or to the
                    communication of informal and tactful oral suggestions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
